@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Language-server provisioning — §8 of the shared entrypoint lib

' covers: packages/lib/entrypoint-lib.sh, defs/opencode/entrypoint.sh,
'         defs/cursor/entrypoint.sh, defs/claudecode/mcp/entrypoint.sh

node "One shared lib, four harnesses" as LIB <<host>> {
  component "**detect** — ""_lsp_walk""\nextension + marker maps → lang·count" as WALK <<app>>
  component "**rank** — awk popularity list" as RANK <<app>>
  component "**eligibility** — ""_lsp_precondition""\ncan this server run HERE?" as PRE <<app>>
  component "**recipe** — ""_lsp_mise_spec""\n· ""_lsp_custom_install""" as RECIPE <<app>>
  component "**install** — ""_mise_install""\nbounded · idempotent" as INST <<app>>
  component "**wire** — ""configure_*_lsp""\nper-harness config format" as WIRE <<app>>
}

component """_proveo_lock_installs""\nflock fd 9" as LOCK <<async>>
database "PROVEO_HOME\n""~/.local/share/mise"" · shims" as HOME <<db>>
cloud "mise registry · ubi → GitHub API\ndownload.eclipse.org" as NET <<cloud>>
component "wrong-arch binary\npasses ""command -v"" · cannot exec" as TRAP <<error>>

WALK ARROW_MAIN RANK : lang<TAB>ftype
RANK ARROW_MAIN PRE : ranked languages
PRE ARROW_MAIN RECIPE : eligible only
RECIPE ARROW_MAIN INST
INST ARROW_QUEUE LOCK : serialize across runs
INST ARROW_CLOUD NET : fetch
INST ARROW_MAIN HOME : install once
HOME ARROW_MAIN WIRE : ""command -v"" finds it
PRE ARROW_ERROR TRAP : the check that prevents this

note right of WALK
  **Separation of responsibilities.** Detection answers //what the workspace
  contains//; it never decides what to install. Eligibility answers //can this
  run on this machine//; it never fetches. Recipes answer //how to obtain it//;
  they never inspect the workspace. Install is the only step that touches the
  network, and wiring is the only step that knows a harness's config format.

  That split is why one lib serves four harnesses whose floors differ: opencode
  and claudecode carry the Node language servers, cursor and cecli carry no Node
  runtime at all, and only the WIRE step differs between them.
end note

note bottom of PRE
  **Eligibility runs BEFORE cost, not after.** ubi will happily install the
  x86_64 clangd on arm64. It then satisfies ""command -v"" and gets wired in as a
  server that dies on first use — worse than never installing it, because the
  failure surfaces to the agent instead of to the installer.

  A post-install health probe was measured and rejected: feeding EOF to healthy
  servers returns 124 (rust-analyzer), 2 (marksman), 1 (taplo/zls/typescript)
  and 0 (terraform-ls/lua/kotlin/bash). No exit code separates healthy from
  broken, so any such probe would discard working servers.
end note

note bottom of RECIPE
  **Two mechanisms, because one does not reach.** ""mise"" is already on the
  floor, so a tool spec costs no new dependency — that covers rust, markdown,
  toml, terraform, lua, zig, kotlin and cpp. jdtls needs a bespoke installer:
  eclipse publishes tarballs rather than GitHub releases, its launcher is a
  python script the Node/Go images cannot run, and its classes are Java 21 while
  the floor's JRE (present for the plantuml jar) is 17.

  A language in NEITHER table is never auto-installed. nil publishes no release
  assets at all, and ruby-lsp needs a source-compiled ruby these images have no
  toolchain for — both are recorded as unreachable rather than silently missing.
end note

note right of LOCK
  PROVEO_HOME is one durable directory shared by every run on the machine, so
  two harnesses starting together race on the same mise tree — which corrupts
  rather than duplicates. Failing to LOCK is not failing to boot: without flock
  it degrades to no locking, and on timeout it skips installs, because the run
  holding the lock is installing the same things anyway.
end note

note right of NET
  ubi resolves releases through the GitHub API — 60 requests/hour when
  unauthenticated, shared PER SOURCE IP, so a fleet behind one NAT hits it
  routinely and loses code intelligence silently. The token is resolved from
  the operator's gh session (see ""_spec/cmd/proveo/github-credentials.puml"")
  and passed to the single install command, never exported to the agent.
end note

note bottom of WIRE
  **Ordering is load-bearing.** Every wiring step gates on ""command -v"", so a
  server installed AFTER the config is rendered stays invisible until the next
  run. opencode and cursor once rendered their config before the installers ran,
  which is why Go intelligence only ever appeared on a second run.
end note
@enduml
